From 913f46aa7d25dc5c37513dc6398bef0588486399 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Hofer <christian.hofer@codasip.com>
Date: Fri, 16 May 2025 14:44:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] examples: Fix examples to build with our libc

We mostly fix cheri-related libc calls that are called differently, e.g.
'cheri_gettag' is called in our musl-libc 'cheri_tag_get'. Other than
that, we replace a few printfs with puts due to stdout buffering.

The following examples are not yet supported:
 * mmap: we miss support for 'cheri_flags_set'
 * seal: uses the non-Linux syscall 'sysctlbyname'
 * sentry: uses 'cheri_sealentry' and 'cheri_flags_set'
---
 allocate.c       |  2 +-
 bounds.c         |  2 +-
 function.c       |  4 ++--
 general_bounds.c | 14 ++++++++------
 include/common.h | 14 ++++++++++++++
 set_bounds.c     | 13 ++++++-------
 setjmp.c         | 11 +++++------
 stackscan.c      | 17 ++++++++---------
 xor_pointers.c   | 13 +++++++------
 9 files changed, 52 insertions(+), 38 deletions(-)

